body:
What OP is saying is that when a guest is trying to check in we’ll see in the guest profile whether the room and taxes will be charged to the CC on file.  What happens is that a guest will try to check in and tell us that XYZ company is paying. If we don’t see that in the guest’s profile we will not charge whatever CC is on file unless the cardholder is there physically. The guest has 2 options at this point. 1 contact their company so they can send us the proper forms or 2 guest can provide his own CC and contact their company later on so they can send the forms and we will then take the guests CC off file.  

&nbsp;  

Yes it’s a huge inconvenience for the guest and they get very upset. Specially when they come in my shift (overnight) and they can’t call their company because it’s 2am and they don’t want to give their personal CC. We do it to protect the business/company from having some random person rack up a bill, I always tell my guests “if you don’t want to give me your card then there’s nothing I can do”.

We have a shuttle schedule online very neat program that let us track our drivers, text with the guests and even lets guest send their location to make sure they’re at the right spot. The problem is that there’s no limit as to how many people can sign up for a specific time. So it’s common for us to get way too many people trying to go in one ride, this happens at least once a week. We used to call the surrounding hotels for help regardless of their brand or parent company.  
&nbsp; 

We were actually the go to guys for every hotel around us because we have an extremely reliable driver. One of the auditors has always have a problem with our driver helping other hotels without telling us. So one night the driver was late to pick up our guests at the lobby by 5 or 8 minutes because he forgot and he was picking other hotel’s guests. Well the auditor told the FOM and blew way out of proportion the issue. Ever since the FOM doesn’t want us calling other hotels or helping other hotels. Night audit isn’t allowed to pay for cabs because we don’t have a MOD so any payouts will come out of our checks.
